Subject: [PATCH 5/7] fix(questions): answer a one-choice form with one button
 per option

A consent such as "Allow searches through the literature sources?" is an MCP
elicitation form with one required choice. It rendered as a "Choice" heading,
a radio list and a separate Send response (live 2026-11-19), so the person
picked a small radio and then pressed a second button. A form that is only one
choice of two or three plain options now shows each option as its own numbered
button; pressing one sends it, and the first is the Enter default. Longer
choices and multi-field forms keep the form.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BHQAws7LSR8fWEJvjbJM4q
